# Two watched discussions have been deleted and one is fine. Each deleted one is
# reported once, not again every minute, and neither stops the healthy thread
# behind them from being checked: after an outage, the round gets through to it
# and CST says so. Polls are a minute apart, so this takes about five.

size 110x30
arg --mux
fake_gh
session app Waiting on a reply
# The fake gh knows no discussion numbered 404.
watch_thread https://github.com/o/r/discussions/404
watch_thread https://github.com/o/s/discussions/404
watch_thread https://github.com/o/r/discussions/7
timeout 150000

wait_for Thread watching cannot read https://github.com/o/s/discussions/404
dump 01-second-deleted-thread

# Any key clears the status line. The next poll finds both still deleted, and
# must not put either message back.
press down
expect_not Thread watching
wait 75000
expect_not Thread watching
dump 02-quiet-a-minute-later

github down
wait_for Thread watching will keep retrying
dump 03-down

# Getting through means reaching the healthy thread, which is listed after the
# two deleted ones.
github up
wait_for Thread watching reached GitHub again
expect_not cannot read
dump 04-reached-again
